<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.10.1: The Vertex and Intercepts of a Function</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02498</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.10.1: The Vertex and Intercepts of a Function</md:title>
    <md:uuid>83cad1cb-379b-4ecf-9269-e4ab1bbb1913</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>These expressions each define the same function.</para>
<list>
  <item> \(x^2+6x+8\)</item>
  <item> \((x+2)(x+4)\)</item>
  <item> \((x+3)^2−1\)</item>
</list>
<para>Without graphing or doing any calculations, determine where the following features would be on a graph that represents the function.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise id="_6f6efa7e-aa7e-4569-8a0f-891502cd7b1b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the \(x\)-coordinate.</para><para>The \(x\)-coordinate of the <term class="glossary-tooltip">vertex (of a graph)</term>.</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex is -3.</para><para>The correct answer is -3. The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex is -3.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_6201a064-001a-4537-9c4a-848ca8f0cc73" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the \(y\)-coordinate.</para><para>The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex (of a graph).</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex is -1.</para><para>The correct answer is -1. The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex is -1.</para></solution></exercise></section>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_380ada69-6116-46ec-b904-b6ac6d41ea2f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para><emphasis>Select both</emphasis> <term class="glossary-tooltip">\(x\)-intercepts</term>.</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(x\)-intercepts are \((-2,0)\) and \((-4,0)\).</para><para>The correct answers are: \((-2,0)\), \((-4,0)\). The \(x\)-intercepts are \((-2,0)\) and \((-4,0)\).</para></solution></exercise></section>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_8dd03ced-8b05-43a1-b1e7-bf429fcbcb0b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the \(y\)-coordinate of the \(y\)-intercept.</para><para>The \(y\)-coordinate of the <term class="glossary-tooltip">\(y\)-intercept</term> \((0, \_\_\_\_\_)\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(y\)-intercept is \((0,8)\).</para><para>The correct answer is 8. The \(y\)-intercept is \((0,8)\).</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
